  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Shepherd's Ledger",
    "overview": "Arashan is a ledger, not a dashboard. A Member opens it in the evening, after the work with the flocks, and records the events of the day: a Lambing, a Sale, a Restock of feed. The interface must take those minutes and give nothing back but the record. It follows the feel of Linear: calm neutral surfaces, exact alignment, small type, fast responses. PRODUCT.md says it plainly: \"The data is the main thing on each screen. The interface does not call attention to itself.\"\n\nThe system is dense but not cramped. Base text is 14px, data is 13px, controls are 32px high and table rows are 36px. The app shell is a quiet canvas with a sidebar on it, and the content sits on one inset surface with a hairline border. Depth comes from tone and lines, not shadows. One green, taken from the highland pastures where the Arashan breed grazes, marks the primary action, the current selection and the focus. Everything else is neutral.\n\nThe system rejects what PRODUCT.md rejects: rustic farm decoration (wood textures, sheep illustrations, hand-drawn fonts), SaaS dashboards with big metric cards and gradients, loud colors and many colored badges, and heavy enterprise ERP forms with dense grids of small fields and many tabs.\n\nThere are two themes, light and dark, and both are first class. The app follows the system setting and lets the Member change it. Motion is restrained: 150 ms state changes with an ease-out curve (`cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1)`), no entrances, no choreography. With `prefers-reduced-motion`, all transitions are instant. In v1 the layout is for a large screen only (from 1024px wide): a sidebar of 240px and a content area that fills the rest.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Neutral surfaces with a faint green tint (chroma 0.003 to 0.005), one green accent.",
      "One type family, Geist, in three weights. Tabular figures in all data.",
      "Flat at rest. Hairline borders and tone separate the layers.",
      "Dense controls (32px) and rows (36px), with generous space between groups.",
      "Keyboard first: each frequent action has a shortcut, and focus is always visible."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Green Rule",
        "body": "Pasture Green appears on 10 percent of a screen at most: the primary action, the selection, the focus. A screen with two green buttons has one too many.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The State Is Not Color Rule",
        "body": "A color never carries a state alone. A Sold Sheep has the word «Продан» next to it; an error has its message under the field.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Pure Gray Rule",
        "body": "Each neutral has chroma 0.003 to 0.01 at hue 150. A pure gray (`oklch(L 0 0)`) is forbidden, except for pure white.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Each number that can sit above another number (a Tag, an amount, a count, a date) uses tabular figures. Columns of numbers that do not line up are a defect.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Caps Rule",
        "body": "No uppercase text with wide tracking, also not in column headers or above sections. Hierarchy comes from weight and color.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat At Rest Rule",
        "body": "A card, a table or a panel on the page has no shadow. If a static surface needs a shadow to stand out, the tones are wrong: fix the tones.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do put the most frequent action of a screen in one Pasture Green primary button, with a shortcut.",
      "Do use tabular figures and right alignment for every number in a column.",
      "Do separate layers with tone and 1px lines: Canvas, then Surface, then Raised.",
      "Do keep every text at 4.5:1 or more in both themes, placeholders included (Ink Muted, 6.0:1 and 6.5:1).",
      "Do keep state transitions at 150 ms with `cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1)`, and make them instant with `prefers-reduced-motion`.",
      "Do check each new screen in the light theme and the dark theme before the merge.",
      "Do show a skeleton while a table loads and a one-line empty state with the action to fill it."
